# Inventory Management System

A Python REST API and CLI tool for managing retail inventory, with integration to the OpenFoodFacts API for fetching real product data by barcode.

## Features

- Flask REST API with full CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete) for inventory items
- Integration with the OpenFoodFacts API to fetch real product details by barcode
- CLI tool to interact with the API (view, add, update, delete inventory, and look up products)
- Input validation and error handling on both the CLI and API layers
- Automated test suite using pytest, including mocked tests for external API calls

## Tech Stack

- Python 3
- Flask
- Requests
- Pytest
- unittest.mock

## Installation and Setup

1. Clone the repository:
```bash
   git clone https://github.com/Mideva-Alma/cli-inventory-management.git
   cd cli-inventory-management
```

2. Create and activate a virtual environment:
```bash
   python3 -m venv venv
   source venv/bin/activate
```

3. Install dependencies:
```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Running the Application

1. Start the Flask API server (in one terminal):
```bash
   python app.py
```
   The server runs at `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.

2. In a separate terminal, run the CLI:
```bash
   python cli.py
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint                          | Description                                  |
|--------|------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| GET    | `/inventory`                       | Fetch all inventory items                     |
| GET    | `/inventory/<id>`                  | Fetch a single inventory item by ID           |
| POST   | `/inventory`                       | Add a new inventory item                      |
| PATCH  | `/inventory/<id>`                  | Update an existing inventory item             |
| DELETE | `/inventory/<id>`                  | Delete an inventory item                      |
| GET    | `/products/<barcode>`              | Fetch product details from OpenFoodFacts      |
| POST   | `/inventory/from-api/<barcode>`    | Fetch a product from OpenFoodFacts and add it to inventory |

### Example: Add an item

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/inventory \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"product_name": "Test Item", "brand": "Test", "price": 5, "stock": 10, "barcode": "999"}'
```

